comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T14:52:15.359Z",pi-agent,"Implemented an open-ended upper bound for synthesized pending release windows while preserving the derived heading date and suppressing a competing leading Unreleased window. npm run build && npm test: 436 passed, 0 failed. npm run coverage: 100.00% lines, branches, and functions. npm run docstring: 12 files and 150 declarations documented. Revert proof: targeted regression exited 1 and placed the release-day item under Unreleased instead of the 2026.8.30 heading. Pre-tag and post-tag generation diff was empty."
  "2026-08-30T15:12:44.500Z",pi-agent,Bot review findings were addressed by making the pending release structurally leading rather than sorting it by its display timestamp. Added regression coverage for a stale timestamp proving the open pending window starts after the newest real tag and cannot overlap. Full npm test remains 436 passed; coverage and docstrings remain 100%.
